course: dictionary
lesson: 11037
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Wean is a good example. «Mum began to wean the baby onto mashed banana» means slowly moving a baby off milk and onto other food. «He is trying to wean himself off sugar» means slowly stopping a habit.
explain: Look at the words around it. In Scotland, «the weans» means the kids, so a sentence about weans in the park is about children. Bairns mean children too, in Scotland and the North East of England. These are regional words, so when you are not sure, check a dictionary.
explain: Grammar gives clues as well. «The wean's ball» has an apostrophe, which shows the ball belongs to one child. The same apostrophe rule works with any noun, such as «the dog's bowl» or «the teacher's desk».
fact: To wean a baby or young animal means to slowly stop feeding it only its mother's milk and start other food.
fact: To wean someone off something means to help them slowly stop needing it, as in «wean off sugar».
fact: In Scotland, a wean is a small child, and «the weans» means the kids.
fact: Wean can be a verb (wean, weans, weaned, weaning) or a noun (a wean).
fact: A good check is to swap in another word: if «child» still makes sense, wean means child.
exercise: «The mother began to wean her puppy onto dog food.» What does wean mean here? | *To slowly stop giving milk and start giving other food | To run very fast | To wash the puppy in warm water | To buy a new bowl
exercise: «She is trying to wean herself off crisps.» What does wean off mean? | To give someone a present | To buy a big bag of crisps | *To slowly stop needing or using something
exercise: «The weans are playing in the park.» What does weans mean? | Grown-up teachers | Baby animals | *Small children | A type of food
test: «The lamb was weaned in May.» What does weaned mean here? | It was born in May | It grew a thick woolly coat | *It began eating other food, not only its mother's milk | It was sold at the market
test: In Scotland, «the wean's ball» means what? | A ball for a grown-up | A ball for football practice | *A ball belonging to a small child | A ball made of wool
exam: Which word in «The weans are ready for their lunch» means small children? | lunch | ready | *weans
